From: Prabhsimran Singh <prabhsimrans@nvidia.com>
Subject: llama: batched greedy argmax outputs

With batched serving, the graph computes one argmax over all output rows for
the greedy sequences instead of per-sequence sampler graphs, and their ids come
back in one copy; only sequences with another sampler get a sampler graph. Output buffers are reserved for the configured
maximum up front, so they are not regrown (and re-pinned) while serving. The
backend top-k sampler uses argmax for k = 1. llama_get_sampled_tokens_ith reads
the sampled ids of many rows after one synchronization.

Upstream: candidate.

